{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbWMjgxy8XhbyLitZ8nP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uyu6eSy3pFf17zLA7inN8e","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/user/.claude/projects/-Users-user-work-delegate-17-claude/4eeac212-2355-47f7-94b7-850a7e176ccd/tool-results/; sed -n 1583,1700p b1iq9x5f2.txt; sed -n 389,700p b1iq9x5f2.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1115,"cache_read_input_tokens":29134,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1115},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eeac212-2355-47f7-94b7-850a7e176ccd","uuid":"a673463d-c890-48e0-8c2f-369dd6bf90be","timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:20:38.947Z","request_id":"req_011CfbWMjKQDmUHddL9AaTGK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Uyu6eSy3pFf17zLA7inN8e":{"command":"cd /Users/user/.claude/projects/-Users-user-work-delegate-17-claude/4eeac212-2355-47f7-94b7-850a7e176ccd/tool-results/; sed -n 1583,1700p b1iq9x5f2.txt; sed -n 389,700p b1iq9x5f2.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uyu6eSy3pFf17zLA7inN8e","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tClaude backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t17\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\ntitle:\tSpec: delegate, a multi-backend CLI replacing the cursor-delegate MCP server\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t4\n--\n## Problem Statement\n\ncursor-delegate lets a host agent hand work to Cursor's models, but only Cursor's, and only from hosts that load its MCP server. The models I actually use are spread across three harnesses: Cursor (Composer, Grok), pi (ChatGPT-subscription GPT models, opencode-go models) and Claude Code (Claude on the Max plan). None of them can reach the others' models.\n\nThe tool has also grown more surface than it uses. Across 413 real `cursor_run` calls, every one ran in the background, `plan` capability was never used, `allowPartialCommit` and `idleMs` were never set, `cursor_wait_any` ran twice, and several parameters (`verifyCommands`, `promptPreamble`, `requireNonClaude`, the `allowUnsandboxed` second signal) only add prompt text or guard against cases that never happen. Eight MCP tools and fourteen run parameters cost schema tokens in every session and make the skill long.\n\nRunning as an MCP server adds its own costs: one resident process per host session, job state that dies with the session, a write lock that cannot see writes from another session, and per-harness registration (Claude plugin, Codex plugin manifest).\n\n## Solution\n\nReplace the `cursor-delegate` MCP server with a CLI called `delegate`, plus one skill. Any harness with a shell can call it. Every configured model is reachable from every harness, routed to one of three backends: cursor-agent, pi, or Claude Code.\n\n`delegate run` starts a job and returns its id immediately. Each job runs under its own detached supervisor that writes a per-job status file. Callers wait with `delegate watch` run in the background and read results from the status file. A finished job can be continued with `delegate resume`. The run surface shrinks to the parameters that real use needs.\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. As an orchestrating agent, I want to start a delegated job with one shell command, so that I can delegate from any harness that has a shell.\n2. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate run` to print the job id and return at once, so that my turn is never blocked on a model.\n3. As an orchestrating agent, I want to pass the prompt on stdin or from a file, so that long briefs need no shell quoting.\n4. As an orchestrating agent, I want to choose a model by id, so that the backend follows from the model without a separate flag.\n5. As an orchestrating agent, I want a default model when I omit one, so that cheap bulk work needs no extra flag.\n6. As an orchestrating agent, I want an unknown model id rejected with the list of valid ids, so that a typo fails fast.\n7. As an orchestrating agent, I want `read-only` and `read-write` capabilities, so that I can say whether a delegate may change files.\n8. As an orchestrating agent, I want `read-only` to be the default, so that a forgotten flag never grants writes.\n9. As an orchestrating agent, I want a pi model with `read-only` rejected, so that I never believe a pi run is read-only when pi cannot enforce it.\n10. As an orchestrating agent, I want to set the delegate's working directory, so that it works in a worktree or scratch directory I prepared.\n11. As an orchestrating agent, I want the working directory to default to where I ran the command, so that the common case needs no flag.\n12. As an orchestrating agent, I want a second read-write job in the same directory refused with BUSY, so that two delegates never interleave edits.\n13. As an orchestrating agent, I want that lock to hold across separate host sessions, so that two Claude sessions cannot collide in one tree.\n14. As an orchestrating agent, I want to give a gate command the tool runs after the agent, so that I get ground-truth verification instead of the delegate's claim.\n15. As an orchestrating agent, I want a failing gate to downgrade DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS with the gate's output, so that I see what failed.\n16. As an orchestrating agent, I want the result to include the git change-set the tool computed, so that I know what actually changed.\n17. As an orchestrating agent, I want a concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty, so that half-committed work is visible.\n18. As an orchestrating agent, I want to widen the tool-call idle window for one job, so that a long build or benchmark is not killed as hung.\n19. As an orchestrating agent, I want a job that goes silent past its idle window killed and reported, so that hung jobs end on their own.\n20. As an orchestrating agent, I want to wait on one or many jobs with `delegate watch` in a background shell, so that my turn can end and I get one notification when they finish.\n21. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate watch` to print every job's final record, so that one command both waits and delivers results.\n22. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate watch` to stop at a timeout, so that a missing or never-written record cannot hang it forever.\n23. As an orchestrating agent, I want to read a job's progress by reading its status file, so that polling needs no tool.\n24. As an orchestrating agent, I want the status file to carry a heartbeat while running, so that I can tell a dead supervisor from a slow job.\n25. As an orchestrating agent, I want the final status file to hold the full result (status, text, usage, cost, change-set, gate result, session), so that the file is the whole answer.\n26. As an orchestrating agent, I want the delegate's final STATUS line to set the result status, including NEEDS_CONTEXT, so that I know when it needs me.\n27. As an orchestrating agent, I want to resume any finished job with a follow-up prompt, so that I can answer a question or ask for fixes without re-briefing.\n28. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to reuse the job's model, directory, capability and gate, so that I cannot forget a setting on the follow-up.\n29. As an orchestrating agent, I want to override capability, gate or model on resume, so that a read-only reviewer can go on to fix what it found.\n30. As an orchestrating agent, I want a model override that crosses backends rejected, so that I never try to resume a cursor session in pi.\n31. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to work after the host session or machine sleep, until reboot, so that follow-ups do not depend on a live server.\n32. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to return a new job id, so that each run has its own record.\n33. As an orchestrating agent, I want to cancel a job by id, so that I can stop a runaway delegate and the commands it started.\n34. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate models` to list ids, labels, backends and prices, so that I can pick a model without reading config.\n35. As a user, I want to see per-run cost, so that I know what delegation would cost at list prices.\n36. As a user, I want cursor runs priced from the model table and pi and claude runs to report their own cost, so that no backend's pricing is reimplemented.\n37. As a user, I want prices for every model in the model table, so that `delegate models` shows them all.\n38. As a user, I want `delegate doctor` to check each backend's binary, version and login, so that setup problems show before a run fails.\n39. As a user, I want doctor to check each configured model is available on its backend, so that renamed or retired models (Grok 4.6 to 4.7) show as warnings.\n40. As a user, I want pi and Claude Code to run with my full configuration (extensions, plugins, skills, context files), so that delegates behave as they do when I run them.\n41. As a user, I want cursor read-write runs unsandboxed, so that delegates can clone, push and open PRs.\n42. As a user, I want Claude Code read-write runs in auto permission mode, so that its classifier still screens tool calls.\n43. As a user, I want Claude Code read-only runs in plan permission mode, so that they cannot edit.\n44. As a user, I want the model list trimmed to models I use, so that the menu is short.\n45. As a user, I want Composer 2.5, Grok 4.7 high and xhigh from cursor; muse-spark-1.3-contributor, glm-5.3-flash, deepseek-v4.1-flash from opencode-go via pi; gpt-6-astra, gpt-6-luna, gpt-6.1-sol from openai-codex via pi; and Claude Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Fable 5.1 via Claude Code.\n46. As a user, I want the project renamed from cursor-delegate to delegate everywhere (binary, config directory, environment variable, status-file directory, skill, repo), so that the name matches what it does.\n47. As a user, I want my existing host profile moved to the new config location by setup, so that my settings survive the rename.\n48. As a user, I want setup to build the binary and put `delegate` on my PATH, so that every harness can call it.\n49. As a user, I want the skill to show briefs that say \"do not delegate further\", so that a delegated Claude does not loop back through delegate.\n50. As a user, I want my global instructions to allow local Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 subagents and route other delegation through `delegate`, so that the Max plan is used where it fits.\n51. As a user, I want the skill to make the background watcher the waiting path, so that agents stop holding turns open.\n52. As a user, I want the skill rewritten for the new surface (catalog, model picks, resume, gates, watcher), so that it stays the single source of usage guidance.\ndiff --git a/src/backends/claude/mod.rs b/src/backends/claude/mod.rs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3b5dfab\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/backends/claude/mod.rs\n@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@\n+//! Claude Code backend: binary, argv, and spawn. Parsing is the shared stream parser.\n+\n+pub(crate) mod doctor;\n+\n+use super::types::Spawned;\n+use crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec};\n+use std::process::Command;\n+\n+pub(crate) fn resolve_bin(r#override: Option<&str>) -> String {\n+    if let Some(o) = r#override.filter(|s| !s.is_empty()) {\n+        return o.to_string();\n+    }\n+    if let Ok(env) = std::env::var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\")\n+        && !env.is_empty()\n+    {\n+        return env;\n+    }\n+    if let Ok(out) = Command::new(\"which\").arg(\"claude\").output()\n+        && out.status.success()\n+    {\n+        let found = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).trim().to_string();\n+        if !found.is_empty() {\n+            return found;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    crate::util::homedir()\n+        .join(\".local/bin/claude\")\n+        .to_string_lossy()\n+        .into_owned()\n+}\n+\n+pub(crate) fn argv(\n+    model: &str,\n+    capability: Capability,\n+    session: Option<&str>,\n+    prompt: &str,\n+) -> (Vec<String>, bool) {\n+    let is_write = capability == Capability::WriteUnsandboxed;\n+    let mut args = vec![\n+        \"-p\".into(),\n+        \"--output-format\".into(),\n+        \"stream-json\".into(),\n+        \"--verbose\".into(),\n+        \"--model\".into(),\n+        model.to_string(),\n+        \"--permission-mode\".into(),\n+        if is_write { \"auto\" } else { \"plan\" }.into(),\n+    ];\n+    if let Some(id) = session {\n+        args.push(\"--resume\".into());\n+        args.push(id.to_string());\n+    } else {\n+        args.push(\"--session-id\".into());\n+        args.push(crate::util::random_uuid());\n+    }\n+    args.push(\"--\".into());\n+    args.push(prompt.to_string());\n+    (args, is_write)\n+}\n+\n+/// Same child driver as cursor: the shared parser reads both stream-json dialects.\n+pub(crate) fn spawn(spec: &JobSpec) -> Spawned {\n+    super::cursor::spawn(spec)\n+}\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+pub(crate) static CLAUDE_BIN_LOCK: std::sync::Mutex<()> = std::sync::Mutex::new(());\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::*;\n+    use crate::backends::cursor::parse_stdout;\n+    use crate::backends::types::BackendResult;\n+    use crate::finalize::{default_finalize_ctx, finalize_run};\n+    use crate::stream::{init_stream_state, parse_line};\n+    use crate::types::{RunStatus, Usage};\n+\n+    fn is_uuid(s: &str) -> bool {\n+        let p: Vec<&str> = s.split('-').collect();\n+        p.len() == 5\n+            && p[0].len() == 8\n+            && p[1].len() == 4\n+            && p[2].len() == 4\n+            && p[3].len() == 4\n+            && p[4].len() == 12\n+            && s.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit() || c == '-')\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn plan_is_read_only_and_auto_is_write() {\n+        let (ask, ask_write) = argv(\"claude-sonnet-5-5\", Capability::Ask, None, \"hi\");\n+        assert!(!ask_write);\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            ask[..8].iter().map(String::as_str).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n+            [\n+                \"-p\",\n+                \"--output-format\",\n+                \"stream-json\",\n+                \"--verbose\",\n+                \"--model\",\n+                \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n+                \"--permission-mode\",\n+                \"plan\",\n+            ]\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(ask[8], \"--session-id\");\n+        assert!(is_uuid(&ask[9]), \"{}\", ask[9]);\n+        assert_eq!(&ask[10..], &[\"--\".to_string(), \"hi\".to_string()]);\n+        assert!(!ask.iter().any(|a| a.contains(\"disallowedTools\")));\n+\n+        let (write, is_write) = argv(\n+            \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n+            Capability::WriteUnsandboxed,\n+            Some(\"sid\"),\n+            \"go\",\n+        );\n+        assert!(is_write);\n+        let pair = |a, b| write.windows(2).any(|w| w[0] == a && w[1] == b);\n+        assert!(pair(\"--permission-mode\", \"auto\"));\n+        assert!(pair(\"--resume\", \"sid\"));\n+        assert!(!write.iter().any(|a| a == \"--session-id\"));\n+        assert!(!write.iter().any(|a| a.contains(\"disallowedTools\")));\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn explicit_override_wins() {\n+        assert_eq!(resolve_bin(Some(\"/custom/claude\")), \"/custom/claude\");\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn env_used_when_no_override() {\n+        let _guard = CLAUDE_BIN_LOCK.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner());\n+        let prev = std::env::var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\").ok();\n+        unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\", \"/env/claude\") };\n+        assert_eq!(resolve_bin(None), \"/env/claude\");\n+        match prev {\n+            Some(v) => unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\", v) },\n+            None => unsafe { std::env::remove_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\") },\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Exit status is not stored in the fixtures. A killed run and a bad model are unclean.\n+    fn clean_exit_for(stem: &str) -> bool {\n+        !matches!(stem, \"error-bad-model\" | \"cancelled\")\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn fixtures_parse_to_a_normalized_result() {\n+        let dir =\n+            std::path::PathBuf::from(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"tests/fixtures/claude\");\n+        let mut files: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(&dir)\n+            .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"{}: {e}\", dir.display()))\n+            .map(|e| e.unwrap().path())\n+            .filter(|p| p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\"stdout\"))\n+            .collect();\n+        files.sort();\n+        assert!(!files.is_empty(), \"no claude stdout fixtures\");\n+\n+        for path in files {\n+            let stem = path.file_stem().unwrap().to_str().unwrap().to_string();\n+            let stdout = std::fs::read_to_string(&path)\n+                .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"{}: {e}\", path.display()));\n+            let stderr = std::fs::read_to_string(path.with_extension(\"stderr\")).unwrap_or_default();\n+            let clean = clean_exit_for(&stem);\n+            let res = parse_stdout(&stdout, clean, &stderr);\n+\n+            assert_eq!(res.clean_exit, clean, \"{stem}\");\n+            assert_eq!(res.stderr, stderr, \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.permission_denials.is_empty(), \"{stem}\");\n+\n+            if stem == \"cancelled\" {\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(true), \"{stem}\");\n+                assert_eq!(res.text, \"no result line\", \"{stem}\");\n+                assert!(res.session_id.is_none() && res.usage.is_none(), \"{stem}\");\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            assert!(res.session_id.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.usage.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.cost_usd.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(!res.text.is_empty(), \"{stem}\");\n+            if stem == \"error-bad-model\" {\n+                // subtype is \"success\"; is_error is what counts.\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(true), \"{stem}\");\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res.text,\n+                    \"There's an issue with the selected model (no-such-model). It may not exist or you may not have access to it. Run --model to pick a different model.\"\n+                );\n+            } else {\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(false), \"{stem}\");\n+            }\n+            if matches!(stem.as_str(), \"plan-edit-request\" | \"needs-context\") {\n+                assert!(res.text.contains(\"STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\"), \"{stem}\");\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"resume-answer\" {\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res.session_id.as_deref(),\n+                    Some(\"25dddfc3-4271-4019-9de0-6795bd6483fa\")\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"auto-fix\" {\n+                let mut state = init_stream_state();\n+                for line in stdout.lines() {\n+                    parse_line(line, &mut state);\n+                }\n+                assert!(state.last_tool.is_some(), \"auto-fix saw no tool call\");\n+                assert!(\n+                    state.files_touched.iter().any(|p| p.ends_with(\"calc.py\")),\n+                    \"{:?}\",\n+                    state.files_touched\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"plan-plain-answer\" {\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res,\n+                    BackendResult {\n+                        text: \"391\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE\".into(),\n+                        session_id: Some(\"25dddfc3-4271-4019-9de0-6795bd6483fa\".into()),\n+                        usage: Some(Usage {\n+                            input_tokens: 2.0,\n+                            output_tokens: 12.0,\n+                            cache_read_tokens: 10261.0,\n+                            cache_write_tokens: 16891.0,\n+                        }),\n+                        cost_usd: Some(0.0697402),\n+                        is_error: Some(false),\n+                        duration_ms: Some(2245.0),\n+                        clean_exit: true,\n+                        stderr: String::new(),\n+                        permission_denials: Vec::new(),\n+                    }\n+                );\n+                let mut ctx = default_finalize_ctx(\"/repo\", \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"claude\");\n+                ctx.git_delta = Some(Box::new(|_, _| None));\n+                let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+                assert_eq!(out.cost_usd, Some(0.0697402));\n+                assert!(!out.cost_estimated);\n+                assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::Done);\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn permission_denials_downgrade_unless_already_error() {\n+        // synthetic: no refusal was recorded in #6\n+        let line = concat!(\n+            r#\"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"blocked\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s\",\"permission_denials\":[{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\"},{\"tool_name\":\"Edit\"}]}\"#,\n+            \"\\n\",\n+        );\n+        let res = parse_stdout(line, true, \"\");\n+        assert_eq!(res.permission_denials.len(), 2);\n+        let mut ctx = default_finalize_ctx(\"/repo\", \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"claude\");\n+        ctx.git_delta = Some(Box::new(|_, _| None));\n+        let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+        assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::DoneWithConcerns);\n+        let concerns = out.concerns.unwrap();\n+        assert!(\n+            concerns\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|c| c.contains(\"Bash\") && c.contains(\"Edit\")),\n+            \"{concerns:?}\"\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(out.permission_denials, res.permission_denials);\n+\n+        let err = concat!(\n+            r#\"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":true,\"result\":\"boom\",\"permission_denials\":[{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\"}]}\"#,\n+            \"\\n\",\n+        );\n+        let res = parse_stdout(err, true, \"\");\n+        let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+        assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::Error);\n+        assert!(out.concerns.is_none());\n+        assert_eq!(out.permission_denials.len(), 1);\n+    }\n+}\ndiff --git a/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs b/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\nindex 9fc6eec..a81205b 100644\n--- a/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\n+++ b/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\n@@ -203,11 +203,12 @@ fn finish(\n             text: raw.result.unwrap_or_default(),\n             session_id: raw.session_id,\n             usage: raw.usage,\n-            cost_usd: None,\n+            cost_usd: raw.cost_usd,\n             is_error: raw.is_error,\n             duration_ms: raw.duration_ms,\n             clean_exit,\n             stderr: stderr.to_string(),\n+            permission_denials: raw.permission_denials,\n         };\n     }\n     // A non-clean exit with no stdout is the bad-model case: the text is the stderr we kept.\n@@ -440,6 +441,7 @@ mod tests {\n                         duration_ms: Some(3279.0),\n                         clean_exit: true,\n                         stderr: String::new(),\n+                        permission_denials: Vec::new(),\n                     }\n                 );\n             }\ndiff --git a/src/backends/mod.rs b/src/backends/mod.rs\nindex 8a8a2ae..435eb73 100644\n--- a/src/backends/mod.rs\n+++ b/src/backends/mod.rs\n@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/user/work/delegate-17-claude","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eeac212-2355-47f7-94b7-850a7e176ccd","uuid":"eb7dcb81-46ed-4254-9bb3-57deb4d64712","timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:20:39.438Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\tClaude backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t17\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nClaude models run through `delegate`. `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose --model ...` with the user's full Claude Code configuration. read-only uses plan permission mode and read-write uses auto mode, or the fallback the probe findings on #4 chose. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume uses `--resume`. Cost is the result line's `total_cost_usd`. Reuse the cursor parser where the streams match. Doctor checks the binary, version and login.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded claude fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error, auto-mode refusal.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake claude replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\ntitle:\tSpec: delegate, a multi-backend CLI replacing the cursor-delegate MCP server\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t4\n--\n## Problem Statement\n\ncursor-delegate lets a host agent hand work to Cursor's models, but only Cursor's, and only from hosts that load its MCP server. The models I actually use are spread across three harnesses: Cursor (Composer, Grok), pi (ChatGPT-subscription GPT models, opencode-go models) and Claude Code (Claude on the Max plan). None of them can reach the others' models.\n\nThe tool has also grown more surface than it uses. Across 413 real `cursor_run` calls, every one ran in the background, `plan` capability was never used, `allowPartialCommit` and `idleMs` were never set, `cursor_wait_any` ran twice, and several parameters (`verifyCommands`, `promptPreamble`, `requireNonClaude`, the `allowUnsandboxed` second signal) only add prompt text or guard against cases that never happen. Eight MCP tools and fourteen run parameters cost schema tokens in every session and make the skill long.\n\nRunning as an MCP server adds its own costs: one resident process per host session, job state that dies with the session, a write lock that cannot see writes from another session, and per-harness registration (Claude plugin, Codex plugin manifest).\n\n## Solution\n\nReplace the `cursor-delegate` MCP server with a CLI called `delegate`, plus one skill. Any harness with a shell can call it. Every configured model is reachable from every harness, routed to one of three backends: cursor-agent, pi, or Claude Code.\n\n`delegate run` starts a job and returns its id immediately. Each job runs under its own detached supervisor that writes a per-job status file. Callers wait with `delegate watch` run in the background and read results from the status file. A finished job can be continued with `delegate resume`. The run surface shrinks to the parameters that real use needs.\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. As an orchestrating agent, I want to start a delegated job with one shell command, so that I can delegate from any harness that has a shell.\n2. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate run` to print the job id and return at once, so that my turn is never blocked on a model.\n3. As an orchestrating agent, I want to pass the prompt on stdin or from a file, so that long briefs need no shell quoting.\n4. As an orchestrating agent, I want to choose a model by id, so that the backend follows from the model without a separate flag.\n5. As an orchestrating agent, I want a default model when I omit one, so that cheap bulk work needs no extra flag.\n6. As an orchestrating agent, I want an unknown model id rejected with the list of valid ids, so that a typo fails fast.\n7. As an orchestrating agent, I want `read-only` and `read-write` capabilities, so that I can say whether a delegate may change files.\n8. As an orchestrating agent, I want `read-only` to be the default, so that a forgotten flag never grants writes.\n9. As an orchestrating agent, I want a pi model with `read-only` rejected, so that I never believe a pi run is read-only when pi cannot enforce it.\n10. As an orchestrating agent, I want to set the delegate's working directory, so that it works in a worktree or scratch directory I prepared.\n11. As an orchestrating agent, I want the working directory to default to where I ran the command, so that the common case needs no flag.\n12. As an orchestrating agent, I want a second read-write job in the same directory refused with BUSY, so that two delegates never interleave edits.\n13. As an orchestrating agent, I want that lock to hold across separate host sessions, so that two Claude sessions cannot collide in one tree.\n14. As an orchestrating agent, I want to give a gate command the tool runs after the agent, so that I get ground-truth verification instead of the delegate's claim.\n15. As an orchestrating agent, I want a failing gate to downgrade DONE to DONE_WITH_CONCERNS with the gate's output, so that I see what failed.\n16. As an orchestrating agent, I want the result to include the git change-set the tool computed, so that I know what actually changed.\n17. As an orchestrating agent, I want a concern when commits landed but the tree is still dirty, so that half-committed work is visible.\n18. As an orchestrating agent, I want to widen the tool-call idle window for one job, so that a long build or benchmark is not killed as hung.\n19. As an orchestrating agent, I want a job that goes silent past its idle window killed and reported, so that hung jobs end on their own.\n20. As an orchestrating agent, I want to wait on one or many jobs with `delegate watch` in a background shell, so that my turn can end and I get one notification when they finish.\n21. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate watch` to print every job's final record, so that one command both waits and delivers results.\n22. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate watch` to stop at a timeout, so that a missing or never-written record cannot hang it forever.\n23. As an orchestrating agent, I want to read a job's progress by reading its status file, so that polling needs no tool.\n24. As an orchestrating agent, I want the status file to carry a heartbeat while running, so that I can tell a dead supervisor from a slow job.\n25. As an orchestrating agent, I want the final status file to hold the full result (status, text, usage, cost, change-set, gate result, session), so that the file is the whole answer.\n26. As an orchestrating agent, I want the delegate's final STATUS line to set the result status, including NEEDS_CONTEXT, so that I know when it needs me.\n27. As an orchestrating agent, I want to resume any finished job with a follow-up prompt, so that I can answer a question or ask for fixes without re-briefing.\n28. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to reuse the job's model, directory, capability and gate, so that I cannot forget a setting on the follow-up.\n29. As an orchestrating agent, I want to override capability, gate or model on resume, so that a read-only reviewer can go on to fix what it found.\n30. As an orchestrating agent, I want a model override that crosses backends rejected, so that I never try to resume a cursor session in pi.\n31. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to work after the host session or machine sleep, until reboot, so that follow-ups do not depend on a live server.\n32. As an orchestrating agent, I want resume to return a new job id, so that each run has its own record.\n33. As an orchestrating agent, I want to cancel a job by id, so that I can stop a runaway delegate and the commands it started.\n34. As an orchestrating agent, I want `delegate models` to list ids, labels, backends and prices, so that I can pick a model without reading config.\n35. As a user, I want to see per-run cost, so that I know what delegation would cost at list prices.\n36. As a user, I want cursor runs priced from the model table and pi and claude runs to report their own cost, so that no backend's pricing is reimplemented.\n37. As a user, I want prices for every model in the model table, so that `delegate models` shows them all.\n38. As a user, I want `delegate doctor` to check each backend's binary, version and login, so that setup problems show before a run fails.\n39. As a user, I want doctor to check each configured model is available on its backend, so that renamed or retired models (Grok 4.6 to 4.7) show as warnings.\n40. As a user, I want pi and Claude Code to run with my full configuration (extensions, plugins, skills, context files), so that delegates behave as they do when I run them.\n41. As a user, I want cursor read-write runs unsandboxed, so that delegates can clone, push and open PRs.\n42. As a user, I want Claude Code read-write runs in auto permission mode, so that its classifier still screens tool calls.\n43. As a user, I want Claude Code read-only runs in plan permission mode, so that they cannot edit.\n44. As a user, I want the model list trimmed to models I use, so that the menu is short.\n45. As a user, I want Composer 2.5, Grok 4.7 high and xhigh from cursor; muse-spark-1.3-contributor, glm-5.3-flash, deepseek-v4.1-flash from opencode-go via pi; gpt-6-astra, gpt-6-luna, gpt-6.1-sol from openai-codex via pi; and Claude Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Fable 5.1 via Claude Code.\n46. As a user, I want the project renamed from cursor-delegate to delegate everywhere (binary, config directory, environment variable, status-file directory, skill, repo), so that the name matches what it does.\n47. As a user, I want my existing host profile moved to the new config location by setup, so that my settings survive the rename.\n48. As a user, I want setup to build the binary and put `delegate` on my PATH, so that every harness can call it.\n49. As a user, I want the skill to show briefs that say \"do not delegate further\", so that a delegated Claude does not loop back through delegate.\n50. As a user, I want my global instructions to allow local Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5 subagents and route other delegation through `delegate`, so that the Max plan is used where it fits.\n51. As a user, I want the skill to make the background watcher the waiting path, so that agents stop holding turns open.\n52. As a user, I want the skill rewritten for the new surface (catalog, model picks, resume, gates, watcher), so that it stays the single source of usage guidance.\ndiff --git a/src/backends/claude/mod.rs b/src/backends/claude/mod.rs\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3b5dfab\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/src/backends/claude/mod.rs\n@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@\n+//! Claude Code backend: binary, argv, and spawn. Parsing is the shared stream parser.\n+\n+pub(crate) mod doctor;\n+\n+use super::types::Spawned;\n+use crate::types::{Capability, JobSpec};\n+use std::process::Command;\n+\n+pub(crate) fn resolve_bin(r#override: Option<&str>) -> String {\n+    if let Some(o) = r#override.filter(|s| !s.is_empty()) {\n+        return o.to_string();\n+    }\n+    if let Ok(env) = std::env::var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\")\n+        && !env.is_empty()\n+    {\n+        return env;\n+    }\n+    if let Ok(out) = Command::new(\"which\").arg(\"claude\").output()\n+        && out.status.success()\n+    {\n+        let found = String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout).trim().to_string();\n+        if !found.is_empty() {\n+            return found;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    crate::util::homedir()\n+        .join(\".local/bin/claude\")\n+        .to_string_lossy()\n+        .into_owned()\n+}\n+\n+pub(crate) fn argv(\n+    model: &str,\n+    capability: Capability,\n+    session: Option<&str>,\n+    prompt: &str,\n+) -> (Vec<String>, bool) {\n+    let is_write = capability == Capability::WriteUnsandboxed;\n+    let mut args = vec![\n+        \"-p\".into(),\n+        \"--output-format\".into(),\n+        \"stream-json\".into(),\n+        \"--verbose\".into(),\n+        \"--model\".into(),\n+        model.to_string(),\n+        \"--permission-mode\".into(),\n+        if is_write { \"auto\" } else { \"plan\" }.into(),\n+    ];\n+    if let Some(id) = session {\n+        args.push(\"--resume\".into());\n+        args.push(id.to_string());\n+    } else {\n+        args.push(\"--session-id\".into());\n+        args.push(crate::util::random_uuid());\n+    }\n+    args.push(\"--\".into());\n+    args.push(prompt.to_string());\n+    (args, is_write)\n+}\n+\n+/// Same child driver as cursor: the shared parser reads both stream-json dialects.\n+pub(crate) fn spawn(spec: &JobSpec) -> Spawned {\n+    super::cursor::spawn(spec)\n+}\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+pub(crate) static CLAUDE_BIN_LOCK: std::sync::Mutex<()> = std::sync::Mutex::new(());\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::*;\n+    use crate::backends::cursor::parse_stdout;\n+    use crate::backends::types::BackendResult;\n+    use crate::finalize::{default_finalize_ctx, finalize_run};\n+    use crate::stream::{init_stream_state, parse_line};\n+    use crate::types::{RunStatus, Usage};\n+\n+    fn is_uuid(s: &str) -> bool {\n+        let p: Vec<&str> = s.split('-').collect();\n+        p.len() == 5\n+            && p[0].len() == 8\n+            && p[1].len() == 4\n+            && p[2].len() == 4\n+            && p[3].len() == 4\n+            && p[4].len() == 12\n+            && s.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_hexdigit() || c == '-')\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn plan_is_read_only_and_auto_is_write() {\n+        let (ask, ask_write) = argv(\"claude-sonnet-5-5\", Capability::Ask, None, \"hi\");\n+        assert!(!ask_write);\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            ask[..8].iter().map(String::as_str).collect::<Vec<_>>(),\n+            [\n+                \"-p\",\n+                \"--output-format\",\n+                \"stream-json\",\n+                \"--verbose\",\n+                \"--model\",\n+                \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n+                \"--permission-mode\",\n+                \"plan\",\n+            ]\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(ask[8], \"--session-id\");\n+        assert!(is_uuid(&ask[9]), \"{}\", ask[9]);\n+        assert_eq!(&ask[10..], &[\"--\".to_string(), \"hi\".to_string()]);\n+        assert!(!ask.iter().any(|a| a.contains(\"disallowedTools\")));\n+\n+        let (write, is_write) = argv(\n+            \"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\n+            Capability::WriteUnsandboxed,\n+            Some(\"sid\"),\n+            \"go\",\n+        );\n+        assert!(is_write);\n+        let pair = |a, b| write.windows(2).any(|w| w[0] == a && w[1] == b);\n+        assert!(pair(\"--permission-mode\", \"auto\"));\n+        assert!(pair(\"--resume\", \"sid\"));\n+        assert!(!write.iter().any(|a| a == \"--session-id\"));\n+        assert!(!write.iter().any(|a| a.contains(\"disallowedTools\")));\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn explicit_override_wins() {\n+        assert_eq!(resolve_bin(Some(\"/custom/claude\")), \"/custom/claude\");\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn env_used_when_no_override() {\n+        let _guard = CLAUDE_BIN_LOCK.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner());\n+        let prev = std::env::var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\").ok();\n+        unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\", \"/env/claude\") };\n+        assert_eq!(resolve_bin(None), \"/env/claude\");\n+        match prev {\n+            Some(v) => unsafe { std::env::set_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\", v) },\n+            None => unsafe { std::env::remove_var(\"CLAUDE_BIN\") },\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Exit status is not stored in the fixtures. A killed run and a bad model are unclean.\n+    fn clean_exit_for(stem: &str) -> bool {\n+        !matches!(stem, \"error-bad-model\" | \"cancelled\")\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn fixtures_parse_to_a_normalized_result() {\n+        let dir =\n+            std::path::PathBuf::from(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"tests/fixtures/claude\");\n+        let mut files: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(&dir)\n+            .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"{}: {e}\", dir.display()))\n+            .map(|e| e.unwrap().path())\n+            .filter(|p| p.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\"stdout\"))\n+            .collect();\n+        files.sort();\n+        assert!(!files.is_empty(), \"no claude stdout fixtures\");\n+\n+        for path in files {\n+            let stem = path.file_stem().unwrap().to_str().unwrap().to_string();\n+            let stdout = std::fs::read_to_string(&path)\n+                .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!(\"{}: {e}\", path.display()));\n+            let stderr = std::fs::read_to_string(path.with_extension(\"stderr\")).unwrap_or_default();\n+            let clean = clean_exit_for(&stem);\n+            let res = parse_stdout(&stdout, clean, &stderr);\n+\n+            assert_eq!(res.clean_exit, clean, \"{stem}\");\n+            assert_eq!(res.stderr, stderr, \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.permission_denials.is_empty(), \"{stem}\");\n+\n+            if stem == \"cancelled\" {\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(true), \"{stem}\");\n+                assert_eq!(res.text, \"no result line\", \"{stem}\");\n+                assert!(res.session_id.is_none() && res.usage.is_none(), \"{stem}\");\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            assert!(res.session_id.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.usage.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(res.cost_usd.is_some(), \"{stem}\");\n+            assert!(!res.text.is_empty(), \"{stem}\");\n+            if stem == \"error-bad-model\" {\n+                // subtype is \"success\"; is_error is what counts.\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(true), \"{stem}\");\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res.text,\n+                    \"There's an issue with the selected model (no-such-model). It may not exist or you may not have access to it. Run --model to pick a different model.\"\n+                );\n+            } else {\n+                assert_eq!(res.is_error, Some(false), \"{stem}\");\n+            }\n+            if matches!(stem.as_str(), \"plan-edit-request\" | \"needs-context\") {\n+                assert!(res.text.contains(\"STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\"), \"{stem}\");\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"resume-answer\" {\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res.session_id.as_deref(),\n+                    Some(\"25dddfc3-4271-4019-9de0-6795bd6483fa\")\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"auto-fix\" {\n+                let mut state = init_stream_state();\n+                for line in stdout.lines() {\n+                    parse_line(line, &mut state);\n+                }\n+                assert!(state.last_tool.is_some(), \"auto-fix saw no tool call\");\n+                assert!(\n+                    state.files_touched.iter().any(|p| p.ends_with(\"calc.py\")),\n+                    \"{:?}\",\n+                    state.files_touched\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if stem == \"plan-plain-answer\" {\n+                assert_eq!(\n+                    res,\n+                    BackendResult {\n+                        text: \"391\\n\\nSTATUS: DONE\".into(),\n+                        session_id: Some(\"25dddfc3-4271-4019-9de0-6795bd6483fa\".into()),\n+                        usage: Some(Usage {\n+                            input_tokens: 2.0,\n+                            output_tokens: 12.0,\n+                            cache_read_tokens: 10261.0,\n+                            cache_write_tokens: 16891.0,\n+                        }),\n+                        cost_usd: Some(0.0697402),\n+                        is_error: Some(false),\n+                        duration_ms: Some(2245.0),\n+                        clean_exit: true,\n+                        stderr: String::new(),\n+                        permission_denials: Vec::new(),\n+                    }\n+                );\n+                let mut ctx = default_finalize_ctx(\"/repo\", \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"claude\");\n+                ctx.git_delta = Some(Box::new(|_, _| None));\n+                let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+                assert_eq!(out.cost_usd, Some(0.0697402));\n+                assert!(!out.cost_estimated);\n+                assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::Done);\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn permission_denials_downgrade_unless_already_error() {\n+        // synthetic: no refusal was recorded in #6\n+        let line = concat!(\n+            r#\"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"result\":\"blocked\\nSTATUS: DONE\",\"session_id\":\"s\",\"permission_denials\":[{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\"},{\"tool_name\":\"Edit\"}]}\"#,\n+            \"\\n\",\n+        );\n+        let res = parse_stdout(line, true, \"\");\n+        assert_eq!(res.permission_denials.len(), 2);\n+        let mut ctx = default_finalize_ctx(\"/repo\", \"claude-sonnet-5-5\", \"claude\");\n+        ctx.git_delta = Some(Box::new(|_, _| None));\n+        let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+        assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::DoneWithConcerns);\n+        let concerns = out.concerns.unwrap();\n+        assert!(\n+            concerns\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|c| c.contains(\"Bash\") && c.contains(\"Edit\")),\n+            \"{concerns:?}\"\n+        );\n+        assert_eq!(out.permission_denials, res.permission_denials);\n+\n+        let err = concat!(\n+            r#\"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":true,\"result\":\"boom\",\"permission_denials\":[{\"tool_name\":\"Bash\"}]}\"#,\n+            \"\\n\",\n+        );\n+        let res = parse_stdout(err, true, \"\");\n+        let out = finalize_run(&res, &ctx);\n+        assert_eq!(out.status, RunStatus::Error);\n+        assert!(out.concerns.is_none());\n+        assert_eq!(out.permission_denials.len(), 1);\n+    }\n+}\ndiff --git a/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs b/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\nindex 9fc6eec..a81205b 100644\n--- a/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\n+++ b/src/backends/cursor/mod.rs\n@@ -203,11 +203,12 @@ fn finish(\n             text: raw.result.unwrap_or_default(),\n             session_id: raw.session_id,\n             usage: raw.usage,\n-            cost_usd: None,\n+            cost_usd: raw.cost_usd,\n             is_error: raw.is_error,\n             duration_ms: raw.duration_ms,\n             clean_exit,\n             stderr: stderr.to_string(),\n+            permission_denials: raw.permission_denials,\n         };\n     }\n     // A non-clean exit with no stdout is the bad-model case: the text is the stderr we kept.\n@@ -440,6 +441,7 @@ mod tests {\n                         duration_ms: Some(3279.0),\n                         clean_exit: true,\n                         stderr: String::new(),\n+                        permission_denials: Vec::new(),\n                     }\n                 );\n             }\ndiff --git a/src/backends/mod.rs b/src/backends/mod.rs\nindex 8a8a2ae..435eb73 100644\n--- a/src/backends/mod.rs\n+++ b/src/backends/mod.rs\n@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/user/work/delegate-17-claude","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
